{"id": "EUVD-2026-108817", "enisaUuid": "10709dec-8af6-3f73-8c5b-61e2c96e07bf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: sequencing: pcie-m2: Fix leaking array from of_regulator_bulk_get_all()\n\nof_regulator_bulk_get_all() allocates the consumers array and hands it to\nthe caller, who is expected to free it at an appropriate time.\npwrseq-pcie-m2.c never did, leading to a memory leak.\n\nAdd an explicit kfree() for the consumers array.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cd2354ebfbd35bcb88d01fe7d3ee08dcf266eff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d6c5794fd633427f0d4ad8b51d94061295649da"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99023"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e8226ae-ed52-3108-8ad6-f560dbc7324a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "535d1558-2d72-34f5-9ee5-57af2bb7629a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "d60394e2-abb2-3b63-b103-8941b5020396", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "dd987e26-6b34-365f-8196-d97c45c83c5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e47d77ae-5f5b-3f1c-afdf-87f3c0e6e191", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52e7b5bd62bab3851f25d8b70ad7eae9e94aba60 <5cd2354ebfbd35bcb88d01fe7d3ee08dcf266eff"}, {"id": "f51889ce-fa48-391d-b13a-b51cea6458c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52e7b5bd62bab3851f25d8b70ad7eae9e94aba60 <0d6c5794fd633427f0d4ad8b51d94061295649da"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2ab4b0f5-37c9-3e12-89fb-58d87cf058f1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}